.TH SMF2WAV 1 "2026-10-05" "VLHE 1.1.0" "VLHE Manual"
.SH NAME
smf2wav \- render a MIDI file to a WAV file through VLHE's synth
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smf2wav
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-q ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR voices | auto ]
.RB [ \-r
.IR rate ]
.RB [ \-g
.IR gain ]
.RB [ \-L
.IR law ]
.RB [ \-F
.IR mode ]
.RB [ \-E " on|off|reverb|chorus]"
.RB [ \-B " on|off]"
.RB [ \-M " fast|reference]"
.RB [ \-s
.IR font.sf2 [@ bank ]]...
.I font.sf2 file.mid out.wav
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B smf2wav
plays a Standard MIDI File through the same synthesizer
.BR vmidid (8)
uses, and writes the result to
.I out.wav
as 16-bit stereo. It opens no sound device, so it works while
something else is playing, and on a machine too slow to play the file
in real time. The control centre's Render MIDI page runs it.
.PP
.I font.sf2
is the base SoundFont, in MIDI bank 0. Each
.B \-s
stacks another font above it, searched first.
.IB font.sf2 @ bank
puts that font's bank 0 in MIDI bank
.IR bank ;
.B "\-s song.sf2@1"
is the usual case, a song that brings its own instruments in bank 1.
Up to seven fonts with
.BR \-s .
.PP
A render ends with the MIDI file, once its last notes and the
effects have died away. A render that runs on past the file's own
length is stopped 30 seconds after it, and no render is longer than about 1.9 GB
of audio - nearly three hours at 44100 Hz. A render stopped either
way says the output is incomplete, and exits 2. A MIDI file too big
for the machine's memory is refused before anything is rendered.
.PP
Options come before the three file names.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
Do not render. Print the estimated length and size of the output, on
standard output, one name and value per line
.RB ( estimate_seconds ,
.BR estimate_bytes ,
.BR rate ,
and
.B capped 1
when the estimate was cut to the 1.9 GB limit), and exit. Loads no SoundFont, but all three file names must still be
given. Only
.B \-r
and
.B \-E
change the estimate.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet: no summary at the end, no progress lines, and no notes about
the SoundFonts as they load.
.TP
.B \-v
Print each voice's envelope, pan and filter cutoff as it starts.
.TP
.BR \-p " \fIvoices\fP|auto"
The most voices at once, 1 to 2048. Default 512 - higher than the
synth daemon's, because a render has no deadline to miss.
.B auto
grows the limit instead of stealing voices, and reports what the file
needed.
.TP
.BI \-r " rate"
The sample rate, 8000 to 46340. Default 44100.
.TP
.BI \-g " gain"
The master gain, 0.001 to 2.0: 1.0 is unity and 0.5 the default.
Whatever is too loud to fit is clipped and counted.
.TP
.BI \-L " law"
The volume curve:
.B spec
(the default), the SoundFont standard; or
.BR linear ,
the gentler Sound Blaster era curve.
.TP
.BI \-F " mode"
The velocity filter:
.B awe
(the default),
.BR 2.01 ,
.BR 2.04 ,
or
.BR none ;
or 1, 2, 3, 0.
.TP
.BR \-E " on|off|reverb|chorus"
Reverb and chorus: on (the default) for both, off for neither,
.B reverb
or
.B chorus
for that one alone. The reverb is nearly all of the effects' cost.
.TP
.BR \-B " on|off"
Filter bypass. Default off. On skips the low-pass filter where its
cutoff is above anything the sample carries, which makes rendering
faster.
.TP
.BR \-M " fast|reference"
The modulation envelope. Default fast, which skips an envelope that
modulates nothing and catches it up exactly when it starts to, and
renders sooner; reference steps it for every voice as the SoundFont
specification describes. Identical on everything tested.
.TP
.BI \-s " font.sf2\fR[\fP@bank\fR]"
Stack another SoundFont, as above.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The file was rendered completely, or
.B \-n
printed its estimate.
.TP
.B 1
A file could not be read or written; a file is not a MIDI file or
SoundFont it can read; the MIDI file is too big for this machine's
memory; there was not enough memory for the voices; or the output
could not be written in full.
A WAV whose write failed is left with its header saying it is
incomplete.
.TP
.B 2
The render was stopped at its ceiling, as above, and the output is
incomplete.
.TP
.B 64
A usage error or an option out of range.
.SH EXAMPLES
Render a file with a General MIDI font:
.PP
.RS
smf2wav gm.sf2 song.mid song.wav
.RE
.PP
Find how many voices a busy file needs:
.PP
.RS
smf2wav \-p auto gm.sf2 song.mid song.wav
.RE
